body: 'Evidence + scripts + raw JSONL preserved in .paradigm/research/warpline-guard-base-rate/ (commit 149e04fa). Hit quality spot-checked: xstate e66662e1 (concurrent generic-signature rewrite × option-type rename in the same traversal functions, git clean) and nest 7c10646a (concurrent logic change + internals refactor of the same SseStream class) are genuine sellable catches; zod d1982eaf is shrug-grade (essence transitivity flagged a symbol whose own text was unchanged). All 17 hits had both sides textually editing the same file(s) — none were cross-file-ripple-only. reducedFidelity ceiling is a non-issue (0.3–4.3% of lifted units). THE OPEN GTM VARIABLE IS PRECISION, NOT BASE RATE: essence-transitivity avalanches flag up to 176 symbols from ~2 directly-contested units (zod types.ts SCC). Next steps named by the experiment: (1) ground-truth the 17 hits (tsc/tests at the merge commit + scan post-merge fixups touching flagged symbols) → convert flag rate into verified catch/false-alarm split; (2) rank direct-contested units above closure ripple to cap per-merge flag volume. Population lesson: merge-traffic composition dominates the observed rate (bot-heavy repos ≈ 0 by construction) — Guard''s target population is human/agent PR merges, which is exactly the wedge.'
